==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|asap}}

===Etymology===
From the {{w|1950's}}. First known use in the book of captain Annis G Thompson, involved in the {{w|Korean War}} titled The greatest Airlift (1954). Originally used in the meaning "as soon as militarily possible" by military forces.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈeɪ.sæp/}}, or as an initialism ({{IPA|en|/ˌeɪ.ɛs.eɪˈpiː/}})
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-ASAP.wav|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|æp|iː|s1=2|s2=4}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{initialism of|en|as soon as possible}}
#: {{antonyms|en|at leisure}}
#: {{ux|en|Susan, please check those figures '''ASAP'''!}}

